# Exclusion-based (REPO-BASELINE §1): deny everything, then admit exactly what a
# .NET image build needs. The inclusion-based alternative ships `web/`, `tests/`
# and `docs/` into every backend build context the first time somebody adds a
# directory and forgets to deny it.
#
# This file serves the builds whose context is the repository root — the .NET
# services. The frontend build has its own context (`web/`) and its own
# `web/.dockerignore`.

*

# The solution's build inputs. `.editorconfig` is one of them, not a nicety: it
# carries analyzer severities, so a context without it compiles under different
# rules than a developer's machine and the build breaks only in CI.
!.editorconfig
!Directory.Build.props
!Directory.Packages.props
!global.json
!NuGet.config
!src/

# ...but never their outputs, which would poison the restore layer and can
# carry a developer's local user-secrets id.
src/**/bin/
src/**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/*.user
